        "title": "History Arc",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Photography's history is the history of making light permanent — first in hours, then minutes, seconds, fractions. Each technical breakthrough democratized photography further: from daguerreotypes requiring trained operators and fixed studios, to the Brownie's \"you press the button, we do the rest,\" to the smartphone where computation substitutes for every technical skill. The arc is not purely one of improvement; each era created distinctive aesthetics that later generations have tried to recover."
    },
