      "text": "THE VIEW FROM THE WINDOW AT LE GRAS (c.1826):\n  Process: bitumen of Judea (light-sensitive asphalt) on pewter plate\n  Camera obscura: focused image of window view at Niépce's estate\n  Exposure time: approximately 8 hours (sun appears to illuminate both sides of\n    courtyard in the image — moved from east to west during exposure)\n  Development: polished with lavender oil + white petroleum → removes unexposed areas"
    },
